,"value":"2026-11-06T05:43:52.202Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"attachGetLinked emits only the selected linked groups: the whole linked selector and depth reads still carry files, tests and docs, while linked.<group> carries only that group, so a present [] always means empty. A new projectGetClaimState selects claim_state.<member> leaves the way schedule.<member> already worked. runGet no longer registers an empty material set for explicit --fields reads. It registers the populated siblings a nested linked, claim_state or schedule selector left out as <facet>.<member>, and resolveGetReceipt renders each with restore_with --fields <facet>.<member>. Null, false and [] siblings withhold nothing and are not listed. GetResult.linked members are optional and claim_state is Partial<ClaimStateContext>; the breaking change is acknowledged in sdk/public-surface.json with a migration line, documented in docs/GET_READ_EVIDENCE.md and recorded on pm-gh1657. The agent-evidence-consistency-control mutant now targets the renamed linked-receipt spec."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Fixed: nested get selectors return only the members they name, and the receipt names the populated siblings they left out"}],"before_hash":"b73fbfcb2c38837eecde50ca6232542213ac6d39de9487dd30875429e1649601","after_hash":"6fcaa53684af881776a2ded77939942254b3e90f3b567dedf09203654ab493fa","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:43:52.202Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f81d385dadf49ee48d8a72c830210c6b8a006ff37607c8f9b55d49c710b3717b"}
